      "extract": "Simplicial volume was defined for manifolds by Gromov in [@gromov:vbc]. For an $n$-dimensional closed manifold $M$ of constant sectional curvature $K=-1$, the simplicial volume $\\|M\\|$ is proportional to the (Riemannian) volume $\\mathrm{Vol}(M)$, and the ratio is the volume of a regular ideal hyperbolic $n$--simplex; in particular, it depends only on the dimension [@gromov:vbc 0.4]. More generally, [@gromov:vbc",
      "extractCut": true
